          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ozone generators do not fix mold. At safe concentrations ozone barely affects it, and at effective concentrations the space must be empty, materials are damaged, hidden growth is untouched and dead spores remain allergenic. Professionals use ozone, if at all, for odor in empty buildings after the mold has been removed.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The fix that works is less dramatic: find and stop the moisture, remove the growth, and run a true HEPA purifier with carbon to clean the air. For the purifier, start with our <a href="/best-air-purifier-for-mold/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">best air purifiers for mold</a>.
